{{/*
   wezterm-only profile: ignore everything in the destination tree that is NOT
   WezTerm config.

   Patterns are matched against TARGET paths via doublestar.Match (NOT
   gitignore semantics). Key consequences:

   - The 'dot_' source prefix is stripped — `dot_config/wezterm/wezterm.lua.tmpl`
     materializes to `.config/wezterm/wezterm.lua`, so the pattern must
     reference `.config/...`, not `dot_config/...`.
   - `*` only matches at one path level. `**` matches at any depth.
   - `!` un-ignores. Order matters: parent directories must be un-ignored
     BEFORE their children for the children to remain visible.

   The `**` rule below also catches `.chezmoiscripts/...` target paths (per the
   header comment), which is what we want: in wezterm-only mode no chezmoi
   script should run — no XDG env vars, no Neovim clone, no Nushell vendor
   regen. The `.chezmoidata/` directory holds template data and never produces
   target files, so it's unaffected by these rules.
*/ -}}
{{ if eq .profile "wezterm-only" -}}
**
!.config
!.config/wezterm
!.config/wezterm/**
{{ end -}}
